WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.000
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Earth...

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Fire...

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Air.

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Long ago, the four nations lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Then everything changed when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Only the Avatar, master of all 4 elements,

8
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.000
could stop them.

9
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.000
But when the world needed him most,

10
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.000
he vanished.

11
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.000
100 years passed,

12
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.000
And my brother and I discovered the new Avatar--

13
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.000
An airbender named Aang.

14
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.000
And although his airbending skills are great,

15
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.000
he has a lot to learn before he's ready to save anyone.

16
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.000
AANG: Oof!

17
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
KATARA: But I believe Aang can save the world.

18
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.000
SOKKA: You guys are gonna be done soon, right?

19
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.000
We've got a lot of ground to cover If we want to make it to Omashu today.

20
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.000
What, like you're ready to go right now, naked guy?

21
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.000
I could be ready in two minutes.

22
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Seriously. Whenever.

23
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
So, you were showing me the octopus form.

24
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Right. Let me see your stance.

25
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Your arms are too far apart.

26
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.000
See, if you move them closer together, you protect your center.

27
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.000
-You got it? -Oh. Yeah.

28
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Thanks.

29
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Ok, let's see what you got.

30
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.000
You make a fine octopus, pupil Aang.

31
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.000
(SPLASH)

32
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
(MUSIC PLAYING)

33
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.000
(MAN HUMMING)

34
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.000
♪ Don't fall in love

35
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.000
♪ With a traveling girl

36
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.000
♪ She'll leave you broke

37
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.000
♪ And broken-hearted

38
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.000
(MUSIC STOPS)

39
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Hey, hey! River people.

40
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.000
We're not river people.

41
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.000
You're not?

42
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Well, then what kind of people are you?

43
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Just people.

44
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Aren't we all, brother? Hoo!

45
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.000
Who are you?

46
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.000
I'm Chong.

47
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.000
And this is my wife, Lily.

48
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.000
We're nomads.

49
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Happy to go wherever the wind takes us.

50
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.000
(SINGS GIBBERISH)

51
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.000
You guys are nomads?!

52
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.000
That's great! I'm a nomad!

53
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Hey! Me, too!

54
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.000
I know.

55
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.000
You just said that.

56
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.000
Oh. Nice underwear.

57
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.000
(GASPS)

58
00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.000
(GRUNTING)

59
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.000
I didn't find anything to eat.

60
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.000
I can't live like this.

61
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.000
I wasn't meant to be a fugitive.

62
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.000
This is impossible!

63
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.000
Uncle...

64
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.000
What are you doing?

65
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.000
You're looking at the rare white dragon bush.

66
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Its leaves make a tea so delicious it's heartbreaking.

67
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.000
That, or it's the white jade bush,

68
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.000
which is poisonous.

69
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.000
We need food, not tea.

70
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.000
I'm going fishing.

71
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Hmm. Delectable tea,

72
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.000
or deadly poison?

73
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.000
(LOWING)

74
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.000
AANG: Hey, Sokka, You should hear some of these stories.

75
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.000
These guys have been everywhere.

76
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.000
Well, not everywhere, little arrowhead,

77
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.000
but where we haven't been,

78
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.000
we've heard about through stories and songs.

79
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.000
They said they'll take us to see a giant night crawler.

80
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.000
MOKU: On the way, there's a waterfall that creates a never-ending rainbow!

81
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Look, I hate to be the wet blanket here,

82
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.000
but since Katara is busy, I guess it's up to me.

83
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.000
We need to get to Omashu.

84
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.000
No sidetracks, no worms, and definitely no rainbows.

85
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:57.000
Whoa! Sounds like someone's got a case of destination fever.

86
00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.000
(LAUGHS)

87
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.000
You're worried too much about where you're going.

88
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.000
LILY: You gotta focus less on the where

89
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.000
and more on the going.

90
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.000
Oh...

91
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.000
Ma...

92
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.000
Shu!

93
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.000
Sokka's right.

94
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.000
We need to find King Bumi so Aang can learn earthbending somewhere safe.

95
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.000
Well, sounds like you're headed to Omashu.

96
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.000
There's an old story about a secret pass...

97
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.000
Right through the mountains.

98
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.000
Is this real or a legend?

99
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.000
Oh, it's a real legend.

100
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.000
And it's as old as earthbending itself.

101
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.000
(STRUMMING)

102
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.000
(HUMMING)

103
00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.000
♪ Two lovers

104
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.000
♪ Forbidden from one another

105
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:42.000
♪ A war divides their people

106
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.000
♪ And a mountain divides them apart

107
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.000
♪ Built a path to be together ♪

108
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.000
Yeah, I forget the next couple lines,

109
00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.000
but then it goes...

110
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:02.000
♪ Secret tunnel

111
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.000
♪ Through the mountain

112
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.000
♪ Secret, secret, secret, secret tunnel

113
00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.000
♪ Yeah ♪

114
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.000
(APPLAUSE)

115
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.000
I think we'll just stick with flying.

116
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.000
We've dealt with the Fire Nation before.

117
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.000
We'll be fine.

118
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.000
Yeah, thanks for the help, but Appa hates going underground.

119
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.000
And we need to do whatever makes Appa most comfortable.

120
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.000
(LOWING)

121
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.000
Launch!

122
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.000
(SNARLING)

123
00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.000
(SCREAMING)

124
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.000
Secret love cave. Let's go.

125
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.000
IROH: Zuko, remember that plant I thought might be tea?

126
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.000
You didn't.

127
00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.000
I did.

128
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.000
And it wasn't.

129
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.000
Aagh!

130
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.000
When the rash spreads to my throat,

131
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.000
I will stop breathing.

132
00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.000
But look what I found!

133
00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.000
These are pakui berries.

134
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.000
Known to cure the poison of the white jade plant!

135
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.000
That, or makaola berries, that cause blindness.

136
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.000
We're not taking any more chances with these plants!

137
00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.000
We need to get help.

138
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.000
But where are we going to go?

139
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.000
We're enemies of the Earth Kingdom,

140
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.000
and fugitives from the Fire Nation.

141
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.000
If the Earth Kingdom discovers us,

142
00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.000
they'll have us killed.

143
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.000
But if the Fire Nation discovers us,

144
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.000
We'll be turned over to Azula.

145
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.000
Earth kingdom it is.

146
00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.000
SOKKA: How far are we from the tunnel?

147
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.000
Actually, it's not just one tunnel.

148
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.000
The lovers didn't want anyone to find out about their love,

149
00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.000
so they built a whole labyrinth.

150
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.000
Labyrinth?!

151
00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.000
I'm sure we'll figure it out.

152
00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.000
All you need to do is trust in love,

153
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.000
according to the curse.

154
00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.000
(GROWLS)

155
00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.000
Curse?!

156
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.000
CHONG: Hey, hey! We're here!

157
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.000
SOKKA: What exactly is this curse?

158
00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.000
The curse says that only those that trust in love

159
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.000
can make it through the caves.

160
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.000
Otherwise, you'll be trapped in them forever.

161
00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.000
And die.

162
00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.000
Oh, yeah, and die.

163
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Hey!

164
00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.000
I just remembered the rest of that song.

165
00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.000
(STRUMS) ♪ And die ♪

166
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:27.000
That's it! There's no way we're going through some cursed hole!

167
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:31.000
Hey! Someone's making a big campfire!

168
00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.000
That's no campfire, Moku.

169
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.000
It's Fire Nation.

170
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.000
They're tracking us.

171
00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:39.000
So, all you need is to trust in love to get through these caves?

172
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.000
That is correct, Master Arrowhead.

173
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.000
We can make it.

174
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.000
Everyone into the hole.

175
00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.000
(SNARLS)

176
00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.000
SOLDIER: Hold on!

177
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.000
It's too dangerous.

178
00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.000
Haven't you heard the song?

179
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.000
Just close them in.

180
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.000
The mountain will take care of the rest.

181
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.000
(GROWLING)

182
00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.000
KATARA: It's ok, Appa. We'll be fine.

183
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.000
I hope.

184
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.000
We will be fine.

185
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.000
All we need is a plan.

186
00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.000
Chong, how long do those torches last?

187
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.000
Um, about two hours each.

188
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.000
And we have five torches, so that's 10 hours.

189
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.000
It doesn't work like that if they're all lit at the same time!

190
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.000
Oh! Right.

191
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:51.000
I'm gonna make a map to keep track of exactly where we've been.

192
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:55.000
Then we should be able to solve it like a maze and get through.

193
00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.000
(APPA GROWLS)

194
00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:06.000
WOMAN: You two must not be from around here.

195
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.000
We know better than to touch the white jade.

196
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:12.000
Much less make it into tea and drink it.

197
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.000
(LAUGHS) Oops!

198
00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:17.000
-So, where are you traveling from? -Yes, we're travelers.

199
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.000
Do you have names?

200
00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:20.000
Names?

201
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.000
Of course we have names.

202
00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.000
I'm... Lee.

203
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.000
And this is my uncle...

204
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.000
Uh, Mushi.

205
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.000
Yes, my nephew was named after his father,

206
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.000
so just call him Junior.

207
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.000
Mushi and Junior, huh?

208
00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.000
My name is Song.

209
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.000
You two look like you could use a good meal.

210
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.000
Why don't you stay for dinner?

211
00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.000
Sorry, but we need to be moving on.

212
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.000
That's too bad.

213
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.000
My mom always makes too much roast duck.

214
00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.000
Where do you live exactly?!

215
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.000
Sokka, this is the tenth dead end you've led us to.

216
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.000
This doesn't make any sense. We already came through this way.

217
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.000
CHONG: We don't need a map.

218
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.000
We just need love.

219
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.000
The little guy knows it.

220
00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.000
Yeah, but I wouldn't mind a map, also.

221
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.000
SOKKA: There's something strange here.

222
00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:12.000
There's only one explanation.

223
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.000
The tunnels are changing.

224
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.000
(RUMBLING)

225
00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:18.000
(CHITTERING)

226
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.000
My daughter tells me you're refugees.

227
00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:25.000
We were once refugees ourselves.

228
00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:29.000
When I was a little girl, the Fire Nation raided our farming village.

229
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.000
All the men were taken away.

230
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.000
That was the last time I saw my father.

231
00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.000
I haven't seen my father in many years.

232
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:42.000
Oh. Is he fighting in the war?

233
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.000
Yeah.

234
00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:53.000
CHONG: The tunnels...

235
00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.000
They're a-changing.

236
00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.000
It must be the curse.

237
00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.000
I knew we shouldn't have come down here.

238
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.000
Right. If only we'd listened to you.

239
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:05.000
KATARA: Everyone be quiet. Listen!

240
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:08.000
(WAILING)

241
00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.000
(SNARLING)

242
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:20.000
A giant flying thing with teeth!

243
00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:23.000
No! It's a wolf-bat!

244
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:34.000
(ROARS)

245
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.000
(GRUNTING)

246
00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.000
(SCREAMING)

247
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.000
(GROWLING)

248
00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:09.000
(PANTING)

249
00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.000
(SCREAMING)

250
00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.000
Yeah, it's no use.

251
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.000
We're separated.

252
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.000
But at least you have us.

253
00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.000
(LAUGHS)

254
00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:20.000
(SCREAMS)

255
00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.000
Can I join you?

256
00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.000
I know what you've been through.

257
00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.000
We've all been through it.

258
00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:38.000
The Fire Nation has hurt you.

259
00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.000
It's ok.

260
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.000
They've hurt me, too.

261
00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.000
(UPBEAT STRUMMING)

262
00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:00.000
♪ Oh, don't let the cave-in get you down

263
00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.000
♪ Don't let the falling rocks

264
00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:06.000
♪ Turn your smile into a frown

265
00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:09.000
♪ When the tunnel's at its darkest

266
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.000
♪ That's when you need a clown

267
00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.000
♪ Hey

268
00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:18.000
♪ Don't let the cave-in get you down, Sokka ♪

269
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.000
Aang, look!

270
00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:28.000
AANG: We found the exit!

271
00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:30.000
(STRAINING)

272
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.000
(APPA GROWLS)

273
00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.000
(SCREAMING)

274
00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:51.000
This isn't the exit.

275
00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.000
No.

276
00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.000
It's a tomb.

277
00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.000
AANG: It must be the two lovers from the legend.

278
00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.000
That's who is buried here.

279
00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.000
These pictures tell their story.

280
00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:31.000
KATARA: They met on top of the mountain that divided their two villages.

281
00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:36.000
The villages were enemies, so they could not be together.

282
00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:40.000
But their love was strong, and they found a way.

283
00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:45.000
The two lovers learned earthbending from the badger-moles.

284
00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:48.000
They became the first earthbenders.

285
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:52.000
They built elaborate tunnels so that they could meet secretly.

286
00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.000
Anyone who tried to follow them

287
00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:57.000
would be lost forever in the labyrinth.

288
00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:01.000
But one day, the man didn't come.

289
00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:06.000
He died in the war between their two villages.

290
00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.000
Devastated, the woman unleashed a terrible display

291
00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:12.000
of her earthbending power.

292
00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:15.000
She could have destroyed them all...

293
00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:19.000
But instead she declared the war over.

294
00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:24.000
Both villages helped her build a new city where they would live together in peace.

295
00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:29.000
The woman's name was Oma, and the man's name was Shu.

296
00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.000
The great city was named Omashu

297
00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:34.000
as a monument to their love.

298
00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:43.000
"Love is brightest in the dark."

299
00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.000
MOKU: Oh, great!

300
00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:50.000
Your plans have led us to another dead end.

301
00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:52.000
SOKKA: At least I'm thinking of ideas

302
00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:56.000
and trying to get is out of here, Moku.

303
00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.000
Whoa, whoa. Wait a minute.

304
00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.000
We're thinking of ideas?

305
00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:01.000
'Cause I've had an idea for, like, an hour now.

306
00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.000
Yes!

307
00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:05.000
We're all thinking of ideas!

308
00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.000
Well, then listen to this.

309
00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:09.000
If love is the key out of here,

310
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:13.000
then all we need to do is play a love song.

311
00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:16.000
(STRUMMING)

312
00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:19.000
AANG: How are we gonna find our way out of these tunnels?

313
00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.000
I have a crazy idea.

314
00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.000
What?

315
00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.000
Never mind. It's too crazy.

316
00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.000
Katara, what is it?

317
00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.000
I was thinking...

318
00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:31.000
The curse says we'll be trapped in here forever

319
00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.000
unless we trust in love.

320
00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.000
Right.

321
00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:37.000
And here it says "love is brightest in the dark"

322
00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.000
And has a picture of them kissing.

323
00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.000
Where are you going with this?

324
00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.000
Well...

325
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.000
What if we kissed?

326
00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:46.000
Us, kissing?

327
00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.000
See? It was a crazy idea.

328
00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.000
Us...

329
00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.000
Kissing.

330
00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:53.000
(SCOFFS)

331
00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:56.000
Us, kissing. What was I thinking?!

332
00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.000
Can you imagine that?

333
00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.000
Yeah. (LAUGHS AWKWARDLY)

334
00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:02.000
I definitely wouldn't want to kiss you.

335
00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:06.000
Oh. Well, I didn't realize it was such a horrible option.

336
00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.000
Sorry I suggested it.

337
00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.000
No, no. I mean...

338
00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:12.000
If it was a choice between kissing you and dying...

339
00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.000
-Oh! -What?!

340
00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:17.000
I'm saying I would rather kiss you than die. That's a compliment.

341
00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:21.000
Well, I'm not sure which I would rather do.

342
00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.000
What is wrong with me?

343
00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:29.000
(STRUMMING TUNE)

344
00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.000
♪ Even if you're lost

345
00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.000
♪ You can't lose the love

346
00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:38.000
♪ Because it's in your heart

347
00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:42.000
♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪

348
00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.000
IROH: Thank you for the duck.

349
00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.000
It was excellent.

350
00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.000
You're welcome.

351
00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:52.000
It brings me joy to see someone eat my cooking with such gusto.

352
00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:55.000
Much practice.

353
00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:58.000
Junior, where are your manners?

354
00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:01.000
You need to thank these nice people.

355
00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.000
Thank you.

356
00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:06.000
SONG: I know you don't think there's any hope left in the world,

357
00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.000
but there is hope.

358
00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:10.000
The Avatar has returned.

359
00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.000
I know.

360
00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:19.000
(LOWING)

361
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.000
What are you doing?!

362
00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:30.000
These people just showed you great kindness.

363
00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.000
They're about to show us a little more kindness.

364
00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.000
Well?

365
00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:53.000
AANG: We're gonna run out of light any second now, aren't we?

366
00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.000
I think so.

367
00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.000
Then, what are we gonna do?

368
00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:59.000
What can we do?

369
00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.000
(STRUMMING)

370
00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:27.000
(GROWLING)

371
00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.000
(SNARLING)

372
00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:40.000
(SCREAMING)

373
00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:46.000
CHONG: Hey! You saved us, Sokka!

374
00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:49.000
No. They were trying to get away from something.

375
00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.000
From what?

376
00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.000
(RUMBLING)

377
00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.000
(GROWLING)

378
00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.000
Aagh!

379
00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.000
Oof!

380
00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:24.000
(CHORD STRUMS)

381
00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:33.000
(CONTINUES STRUMMING)

382
00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:36.000
Hey, those things are music-lovers!

383
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:39.000
♪ Badger-moles coming towards me

384
00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:40.000
♪ Come on, guys

385
00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.000
♪ Help me out

386
00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.000
♪ The big bad badger-moles

387
00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.000
♪ Who opened the tunnels

388
00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.000
♪ Hate the wolf-bats

389
00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:50.000
♪ But love the sounds ♪

390
00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:53.000
AANG: It's made of some kind of crystals.

391
00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.000
They must only light up in the dark.

392
00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:57.000
That's how the two lovers found each other.

393
00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:01.000
They just put out their lights and followed the crystals.

394
00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:05.000
That must be the way out!

395
00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:09.000
So, um...

396
00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.000
Let's go!

397
00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.000
(GROWLS)

398
00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:31.000
What about Sokka?!

399
00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:34.000
(RUMBLING)

400
00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.000
(SNARLING)

401
00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:40.000
Sokka!

402
00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:43.000
How did you guys get out?!

403
00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:45.000
Just like the legend says--

404
00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:46.000
We let love lead the way.

405
00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:50.000
Really? We let huge ferocious beasts lead our way.

406
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:55.000
(GROWLING)

407
00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:00.000
(CHITTERING)

408
00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:04.000
(ROARS)

409
00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.000
Why is your forehead all red?

410
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:12.000
Nobody react to what I'm about to tell you.

411
00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:13.000
I think that kid

412
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:16.000
might be the Avatar.

413
00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:22.000
AANG: So, are you guys gonna come to Omashu with us?

414
00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:23.000
-Nope. -Ok.

415
00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:26.000
Thanks for everything, Moku.

416
00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:28.000
Sokka,

417
00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:31.000
I hope you learned a little something about not letting the plans

418
00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:34.000
get in the way of the journey.

419
00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:37.000
Just play your songs.

420
00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:39.000
Hey! Good plan!

421
00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:42.000
(STRUMMING)

422
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.000
♪ Even if you're lost

423
00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:47.000
♪ You can't lose the love

424
00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:51.000
♪ Because it's in your heart

425
00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:56.000
♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪

426
00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:59.000
SOKKA: The journey was long and annoying,

427
00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:01.000
but now you get to see what it's really about--

428
00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:03.000
The destination.

429
00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:04.000
I present to you

430
00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:07.000
the Earth Kingdom city of O--

431
00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:10.000
Oh, no!

432
00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:24.000
(MEN CHANTING RHYTHMICALLY)

